{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושמחת בכל הטוב", :translit "v'samachta b'chol ha-tov", :gloss "and you shall rejoice in all the good"} {:he "כי תכלה לעשר", :translit "ki t'chaleh la'aser", :gloss "when you finish tithing"} {:he "עשר", :translit "aser", :gloss "tithe"} {:he "בשביל שתתעשר", :translit "b'shvIL sh'tit'aser", :gloss "so that you may become rich"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic pun: עשר (tithe) read as בשביל שתתעשר (so that you become rich)"}], :frame {:text "The Sages expounded the word עשר (tithe) as a promise: בשביל שתתעשר, 'so that you may become rich' — tithing leads to wealth (Taanit 9a). Ba'al HaTurim applies this to the adjacency of Deuteronomy 26:11 to Deuteronomy 26:12: rejoicing in 'all the good' comes specifically through the act of tithing.", :sources ["Taanit 9a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הטוב", :translit "ha-tov", :gloss "the good"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "הטוב", :b "כב אותיות"}], :frame {:text "The Torah is composed of 22 letters, corresponding to the 22 letters of the Hebrew alphabet (Sefer Yetzirah 1:1). All of creation and revelation are encompassed within these letters, as stated: 'With twenty-two letters God engraved and formed all that is' (Sefer Yetzirah 1:1).", :sources ["Sefer Yetzirah 1:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic pun: עשר (tithe) read as בשביל שתתעשר (so that you become rich)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "הטוב", :a-value 22, :b "כב אותיות", :b-value 845, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:28.463913095Z", :model "glm-5.2"}